WEBVTT

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.380
Sorry. If we didn't do this, we'd vanish.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.910
So, there really were other
ethereal spirits like ourselves.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.210
Let go of Arashi-san!

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.510
Be a good boy and don't move.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.020
Or you're dead.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:34.880
Just a bit more...

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.410
I see.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.160
Shades...

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.690
Jeez, what the hell are you thinking?

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.520
Were you really going to kill him?

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.080
Who knows?

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.170
I hate that kind of shit.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.830
Our contract is canceled, miss.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.570
I see. So what?

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:18.920
Arashi-san!

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:23.750
You attacked a woman.
Guys are such beasts in every era.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.000
Damn it...

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.810
Arashi-san! Arashi-san!

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:29.520
That war, too. It was started by selfish men.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:33.550
And thanks to them, we ended up like this.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:37.490
I don't even want to remember it. That horrible raid...

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.060
The way flares poured from the sky...

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.350
Arashi-san!

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.370
Investigate us, and I'll kill you.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.590
Tell the police, and I'll kill you.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:48.580
Got it?

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:50.260
Goodbye, then.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:51.090
Wai-

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.860
Damn it...

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:00.610
Foreigner - Kaya

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.910
Hey, tell me already.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.900
What are they?

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.300
Ghosts.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.740
They've kept on living for the past sixty years.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.260
Ghosts, huh?

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.730
Hey, Shades.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.730
Take me to that woman.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.520
And what will you do to her?

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.120
She's the kind of woman who carries a crossbow in her skirt.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.360
You've gotta tell the cops.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.280
Tell 'em what?

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.800
If they found out about her...

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:43.050
Arashi-san relied on a kid like me because she wanted to avoid that!

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.250
And yet...

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:45.760
Kid...

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.450
I can't protect her even once?

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.970
No way!

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:53.200
Fine, fine.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.510
Let's go.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.890
Why are you coming with me?

00:04:57.890 --> 00:04:59.760
Who the hell are you, anyway?

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.870
The hell you say?

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.520
Man, you're a bratty kid!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.610
Trust me.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:10.650
This is my card.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.280
Private Detective Murata Hideo

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.290
I'm a private detective.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:16.010
Murata Hideo...

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.990
Your name's Murata Hideo?

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:27.240
Yeah. The name comes from a hero who saved my dad during the bombing.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.940
"Be a hero."

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:31.000
Fits me perfectly, doesn't it?

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.620
I see... I see.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:38.280
Arashi-san wasn't wrong at all.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:45.810
The people she saved existed before she saved them!

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:47.860
What are you talking about?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.070
History didn't change at all.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:56.820
No, more accurately, her having saved them made this time what it is.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.140
Nobody's vanished!

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:00.490
Nobody's been sacrificed!

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:05.880
Arashi-san, you were a true hero.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:15.910
All right! Let's go find her, Shades!

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:18.550
Don't try to take the lead.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.320
Wait for me, Arashi-san.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.620
I'm sorry. I didn't read anything today.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.330
Rest well.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.330
This is life for you.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.130
There.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.520
What's it like inside?

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.080
I've only been in there a few times.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.480
But it's always dark, like a haunted house.

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.430
I've never seen any parents.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:19.510
The only ones were that scary bitch, Yamazaki Kanako,

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:23.660
and a girl, about her age,
whose name I don't even know.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:28.990
What kind of girl?

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:31.300
A quiet type, in a wheelchair.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.970
They seemed like good friends.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.620
Probably someone the black woman connected with.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.310
So, what will you do?

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.410
You should have a plan.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:45.020
She uses some weird tricks. She'll be pretty tough.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.800
Inside, we should split up.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.560
You going it alone?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:50.670
Isn't that dangerous?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.680
You draw the black woman's attention.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:57.360
I'll find the other and take her hostage.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.030
Hey, isn't that going a bit far?

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.670
I don't want to take a girl in a wheelchair hostage.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.510
They did it to Arashi-san!

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:11.040
Well?

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.690
How is she?

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:22.940
Is that what you talked about this afternoon?
Her existence becoming unstable or whatever?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.160
Probably.

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:25.950
So, what's going on?

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.100
What did Hajime say?

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:28.970
Nothing specific.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:33.530
Jeez, that kid... He should talk to an adult before he does shit.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:38.990
He doesn't want other people to find out about Arashi-san or Kaya-san.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:41.240
Am I "other people"?

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:44.810
Well, whatever.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.760
Anyway, want to make something to eat?

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.320
What are you talking about, at a time like this?

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:55.580
Hajime's gonna do something to make her better, right?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:09:02.060
So when she wakes up, we need to all be happy and energetic, too.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:08.310
I'll ask his grandfather if we can borrow the kitchen.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.510
Yeah, and some beer!

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:23.050
Man, steamy in here...

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.290
Aren't they hot?

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.850
You're pretty fucking scary looking.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.850
I'm not scary looking! I'm angry!

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:38.310
Make sure not to lose that.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.250
Let's split up and check different floors.

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.680
I'll check the upstairs.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:48.170
OK. I'll pray you don't run into the scary chick.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.270
Man, ghost-busting?

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:56.270
Natsu no Arashi

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:01.070
Huh, nice stuff here.

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:04.950
What kind of life do they live, I wonder?

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:13.420
This is pretty old, too...

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:23.780
No one?

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:31.270
She doesn't even make a sound?

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:33.530
Man, we shouldn't have come at night.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:51.840
This is the black woman's friend.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:57.410
Who's there?

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:10.300
Hell yeah!

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:13.660
Someone from WWII has probably never seen this before!

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:28.200
Damn it. This is just bullying.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.000
Come on.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:33.740
Stand up.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:48.170
Even somebody from the war knows about these.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.090
I'm tying you up.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:03.810
Sorry, I can't show you any mercy.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:05.760
Kanako?

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:06.820
Where's Kanako?

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:08.970
What happened? What happened?

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:10.210
Where's Kanako?

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:13.800
You connected with her, didn't you?

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:14.910
What?

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:19.840
Hey, did she threaten you into making you do what she wants?

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:20.940
Me?

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.120
By Kanako?

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:23.430
She did, didn't she?

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.960
I'll help you. Let's get out of here!

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:26.860
No!

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:27.980
What are you talking about?

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.870
You're completely wrong!

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.310
Kanako wouldn't do that.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.700
I know she's important to you,

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.000
but it doesn't matter.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.880
She came after us first.

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:46.830
You're coming with me.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.550
You're turning Arashi-san back to normal.

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.740
You're Arashiyama-san's...

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.190
You know her, too?

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:58.930
What?

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.550
What are you?

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.290
Don't touch me!

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.050
What's going on?

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:22.500
I...

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:26.810
We went to the same school as her.

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:27.910
What?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:31.150
My name is Fushimi Yayoi.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:36.910
Natsu no Arashi - Master

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.930
Showa 20 (1945)

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:50.520
Hey, did you hear it, Fushimi-san?

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:54.030
Arashi's rendition of
"A Song of Early Spring" was wonderful!

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:55.010
Yeah.

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:58.270
It was totally different from our "If I Go Away to the Sea."

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:01.340
I like when she sings Lorelei with Kaya-san!

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:04.100
Yeah, Kaya's good, too.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:05.740
How about you, Fushimi-san?

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.000
I...

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:14.080
Good morning, everyone.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.590
Good morning.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:29.100
Wow... When Arashi and Kaya are together, it's like a movie.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:33.310
Yeah. I can't wait for the next recital.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.470
Oh right, Fushimi-san!

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:38.670
I heard they asked you to do their accompaniment?

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.520
Oh, yeah.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.930
You're good at piano.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:44.580
I'm so jealous!

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:48.100
I don't know if I can do it.

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:50.070
But I'll do my best!

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.720
I can't wait!

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.110
You girls there!

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.110
How long will you stand around talking?

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.660
I'm sorry.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:02.510
Don't do crappy work because you're daydreaming

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:07.210
over a bunch of girls who can't even tie their hair,
and then expect us to pick up your slack.

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:10.570
Jeez, what was that?

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:11.720
She's just jealous!

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:15.210
She's mad because she has to work in the factories.

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:23.070
Who cares if they're from money?

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.820
Who cares if they're university students?

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:29.700
They're totally useless!

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:39.590
You're...

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:41.920
Let me help you.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:16:00.600
How wonderful it would be if I practiced a lot and Arashi praised me!

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.610
Fushimi-san?

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.960
Ah, umm...

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.190
Yamazaki.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:11.650
Yamazaki-san...

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.210
You're pretty full of yourself.

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:21.250
I'd expect no less from a university student.

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:26.460
You quit work early, and you have time to play the piano?

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.120
What? No...

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.430
I don't like you.

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:33.130
You think if you act like a good girl,
people will treat you well?

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.860
That sound hurts my ears.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:39.350
Tear that piano apart and donate the wire to the war effort!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.450
Um...

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:51.720
If you'd like, would you come to the concert
on the next scheduled power outage?

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.900
I think it will be a lot of fun!

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:56.280
We can all go back to being girls, kind of...

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:01.040
Are you making fun of me?

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.260
No.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:03.800
I won't even consider going!

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:12.460
But Kanako came.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.790
She listened to my song.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:19.360
Why would a bitch like that suddenly decide to go?

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:20.840
What happened?

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:22.810
I don't know.

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:26.390
But she's really a kind girl.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.370
She doesn't look it.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:30.690
It's true.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:36.480
After the concert, we got to talking, and we got along surprisingly well.

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.850
And she opened up to my other friends.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:43.040
And ever since then, we've supported one another.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:49.790
During those dark, horrible days when we were conscripted...

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:52.720
And even now.

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:56.810
What are you doing here?

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.050
Kanako!

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.260
It's OK, Kanako.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:05.350
He didn't do anything to me.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:06.570
You...

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:07.990
Kanako, please?

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:10.280
Stop this already!

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:14.010
It's fate that we're disappearing.

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:18.310
No, I think it's actually better this way.

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:20.570
Everybody else, they all died that day...

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:25.040
I can't accept such an unfair way to die.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.700
Live, Yayoi.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:28.790
The two of us must survive, no matter what!

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:33.150
Even to the point of sacrificing Arashi-san?

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:35.250
She has things she has to do!

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:38.760
She's going back in time to save lots of people from the air raids,

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:40.470
not even thinking of the danger to herself!

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:46.050
Wonderful. Oh, what a wonderful person she is, in every era.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.770
Kanako...

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:52.990
If that's true, then she would've been happy to sacrifice herself for us.

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:54.600
I won't let that happen!

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:57.760
She wants to save people, doesn't she?

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:02.250
That may be what she feels is right,

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:04.300
but I don't think so!

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:10.890
I think what's right is for me to help Arashi-san go back sixty years and protect her!

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:19.930
Did you go to April 29th, 1945?

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:23.270
April... 29th...

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.580
No?

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:28.460
That's why you can still say that.

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:35.280
Ever since that day, Yayoi's been so scared, she can't even walk.

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:46.310
I will never... Never let her be scared again.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:50.700
We will live in peace until the end of eternity!

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:56.240
And anybody who gets in our way will die!

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.040
I can't die here!

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.480
Ow...

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:27.440
Where... Where did you go?

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:28.150
Yayoi!

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:29.180
Yayo-

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.960
<i>Yayoi!</i>

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:20.390
Bored.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:24.100
Bored...

00:22:30.170 --> 00:22:32.710
Anything interesting to talk about?

00:22:33.970 --> 00:22:38.110
Um, I read a book a while ago.

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:40.980
What was it called?

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:43.620
Well, I forgot the title.

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:46.230
Tell me what kind of story it was.

00:22:46.230 --> 00:22:47.400
Yes.

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:52.560
It was the story of a very peaceful school.

00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:55.090
The students are divided into a vast number of teams.

00:22:55.090 --> 00:22:58.730
They mature and grow-sometimes fighting, sometimes friends.

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:01.940
And each takes advantage of their unique attributes.

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:06.140
The main character belongs to an especially well-known team,

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:09.200
and all their minds are filled with avant-garde ideas.

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.820
Huh, interesting.

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:14.660
This team had a phrase they would always say.

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:16.250
What was it?

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:20.240
<i>Kimen-</i>

00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:21.360
<i>Flash!</i>

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:22.360
Right?

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:25.750
Arashi!

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.170
Is she OK?

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.920
Did I do something wrong?

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:32.500
When you think of summer-

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:33.750
You think of rain, I guess.

00:23:33.750 --> 00:23:37.410
It starts suddenly, and if you buy an umbrella at the convenience store, it stops.

00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:38.920
Don't you end up with a bunch of umbrellas, then?

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:41.260
No, I keep losing them, so it evens out.

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:44.090
Get up bright and early tomorrow!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.150
<i>Get up bright and early tomorrow!</i>

